Drop the pid from the sway IPC socket path

REG-Linux hardcodes the socket location in
package/frontend/regstation/wayland/sway/04-sway.sh:

    export SWAYSOCK="$runtime_dir/sway-ipc.0.sock"

That profile script runs for every login shell and cannot know sway's pid,
so upstream's "%s/sway-ipc.%u.%i.sock" would leave SWAYSOCK pointing at a
socket that does not exist and break swaymsg everywhere. Only one sway
instance runs on these images, so dropping the pid is safe.

Note: this patch used to be called 000-allow-running-as-root.patch and also
carried three hunks against sway/main.c that neutered detect_suid(). sway
1.12 removed the SUID check upstream (no detect_suid() remains in main.c),
so running as root needs no patch any more and those hunks are gone. Keeping
them would not merely have been dead weight -- the third hunk still applied
with fuzz and re-inserted a call to the now-deleted function, which would
have failed to compile.

Signed-off-by: REG-Linux <reglinux@reglinux.org>

--- a/sway/ipc-server.c
+++ b/sway/ipc-server.c
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@
 		dir = "/tmp";
 	}
 	if (path_size <= snprintf(ipc_sockaddr->sun_path, path_size,
-			"%s/sway-ipc.%u.%i.sock", dir, getuid(), getpid())) {
+			"%s/sway-ipc.%u.sock", dir, getuid())) {
 		sway_abort("Socket path won't fit into ipc_sockaddr->sun_path");
 	}

